  "description": "Reed-Solomon erasure coding for .NET in pure managed C#: no native libraries, no P/Invoke, no dependencies. SIMD accelerated GF(2^8) kernels (GFNI, AVX-512, AVX2, SSSE3, ARM NEON) with register blocking and Span overloads that let encode and verify run without allocating. Encode data into data + parity shards, verify them, and reconstruct any missing shards; parity is byte-compatible with Backblaze JavaReedSolomon, klauspost/reedsolomon and reed-solomon-erasure. A fully managed, AOT-friendly alternative to Intel ISA-L wrappers for storage, backup, RAID-like striping and network FEC.",
